These data details the trajectories of 5 surface drifters deployed with drogue during an adaptative sea survey campaign referred to as "BOBLIT1.0 - Adaptative survey"

Buoys used are a set of cylinder-shaped home-made drifters with drogue.

These buoys were equipped with an anchor of 0.5 m long positioned in the water column between 0.8 and 1.3 m depth, allowing them to drift with surface currents. 

Reference time: local

To get a first look at the trajectories, visit: https://aztidata.es/ebegi/ (Platform type: "Drifters")
